{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/273146-two-world-eyes-and-dual-senses","id":273146,"title":"Two-World Eyes and Dual Senses","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-10-05T12:40:45-07:00","id":273146,"title":"Two-World Eyes and Dual Senses","content":"Since I haven't seen any errata, ruling, or anything even semi-official regarding this gift and rule I have come to ask this in the forum. The question is, how does the Two-World Eyes gift interact with the Dual Senses rule?<br /> <br /> My original interpretation was that one eye stays with your body in whatever realm you're standing, while the other sees the other side of the gauntlet as if it were there and thus has no penalties to vision. It would see clearly the other side as if the werewolf was standing on the other side. This being separate from the standard method of looking sideways which would involve actually looking through the Gauntlet.<br /> <br /> My storyteller disagrees, and states that Two-World Eyes still suffers the penalty of looking through the Gauntlet and your vision would still be cloudy and indistinct. This also leads me to ask whether the exceptional success of Two-World Eyes would even see clearly since it doesn't actually say that it would, only that you gain additional perception forms (smell or sound) which would also presumably be indistinct and muddled.<br /> <br /> I was told if I could find errata or something on the forums he might reconsider this ruling. So, since I haven't found anything I figured I'd ask the forums and see if anyone has anything to say on this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4004-durionarcanis","name":"DurionArcanis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-05T13:16:35-07:00","id":273181,"title":"","content":"Plain and simply, your storyteller's interpretation is incorrect. If that was the case, such modifiers would have been addressed somewhere in the gift's write-up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-05T19:01:39-07:00","id":273403,"title":"","content":"The thing is, it neglects to say one way or the other. Since it doesn't say it is separate, and it doesn't it still suffers from them, it's completely up to reader interpretation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4004-durionarcanis","name":"DurionArcanis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-06T03:22:34-07:00","id":273557,"title":"","content":"You'll note that the power explicitly states you are subject to the normal penalties for looking over the Gauntlet on a Dramatic Failure - implicitly indicating that the penalties in question do <i>not</i> apply on other results of the Gift's use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-06T15:23:29-07:00","id":274196,"title":"","content":"I did notice that, unfortunately I'm not sure it's enough to convince my ST even having others support and point it out yet. But it does help my case at least.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4004-durionarcanis","name":"DurionArcanis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-07T01:19:15-07:00","id":274565,"title":"","content":"From the Two-World Eyes entry: &quot;Success: The character can see and understand what is happening on both sides of the Gauntlet <b>without penalty</b>.&quot;<br /> <br /> From the fluff for Two-World Eyes, &quot;Ithaeur, however, can peer across the line between worlds <b>without sacrificing their perception of either one</b>.&quot; (emphasis added)<br /> <br /> If an Ithaeur using Two-World Eyes still had their vision obscured by the Dual Senses rules, what kind of penalty is it that Two-World Eyes eliminates? What else could the benefit of Two-World Eyes even be?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3755,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3755-jaerys","user":"Jaerys","date":". 10-07-2014, 04:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3755-jaerys","name":"Jaerys","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-07T07:04:03-07:00","id":274701,"title":"","content":"Well, it's entirely up to the Storyteller, in how they want to run it, but for clarity's sake, All werewolves can peek across the gauntlet with Dual Senses, but it is the Ithaeur who is most designed to look through both worlds hence the Two-World eyes gift. This gift is meant to enforce that fact of the Ithaeur and so he/she is not penalized by the Dual Senses rule when they use this gift. The gift's activation roll may still be penalized by the Gauntlet Strength in the area but the Ithaeur's actual senses are not penalized. They can see perfectly clearly while using this gift. That's my interpretation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3777-the-scorpion","name":"The Scorpion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-07T11:48:18-07:00","id":274894,"title":"","content":"How about Chris' word as a writer? I would think that would be enough to sway most folk.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-07T23:19:15-07:00","id":275221,"title":"","content":"Having one of the writers chime in on it should certainly convince him, I've been keeping him updated loosely on updates and info I find but I haven't tried to appeal my case yet with him formally. Though I may attempt to do so again before the next session on Sunday.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4004-durionarcanis","name":"DurionArcanis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-08T11:10:54-07:00","id":275579,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DurionArcanis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/273146-two-world-eyes-and-dual-senses?p=275221#post275221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having one of the writers chime in on it should certainly convince him, I've been keeping him updated loosely on updates and info I find but I haven't tried to appeal my case yet with him formally. Though I may attempt to do so again before the next session on Sunday.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's Acrozatarim up over there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-08T19:01:40-07:00","id":275972,"title":"","content":"Oh! Well then. I had no idea. I blame it on the fact that I'm such a bloody noob here :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4004-durionarcanis","name":"DurionArcanis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-09T02:52:27-07:00","id":276150,"title":"","content":"To be fair, I'm a writer on Forsaken 2nd Edition. While I've written almost all the 2e Gifts I didn't write the ones for 1e.<br /> <br /> However, it seems painfully obvious to me that Two World Eyes is supposed to offer clear perception of the other side of the Gauntlet and, certainly, when I initially wrote the new Crescent Moon Gifts, I kept that element in as part of one Facet. Then it turned out that wasn't necessary, but that's another spoiler for another day <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-09T07:08:39-07:00","id":276288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/273146-two-world-eyes-and-dual-senses?p=276150#post276150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, I'm a writer on Forsaken 2nd Edition. While I've written almost all the 2e Gifts I didn't write the ones for 1e.<br /> <br /> However, it seems painfully obvious to me that Two World Eyes is supposed to offer clear perception of the other side of the Gauntlet and, certainly, when I initially wrote the new Crescent Moon Gifts, I kept that element in as part of one Facet. Then it turned out that wasn't necessary, but that's another spoiler for another day <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Ugh, you people are so good at this <i>teasing</i> thing. &gt;:/","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-09T07:18:19-07:00","id":276299,"title":"","content":"Considering the Shaman template could automatically look into twilight without turn-long rolls, I guess that's the right approach.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}